2	 * SFCC-83/84 build plan step A6 — asserts only this component's own branch-selection contract
3	 * (`.claude/rules/testing.md`'s no-duplicate-coverage rule): given a `recommender` and
4	 * `useRecentlyViewedHistory`'s return value, does it render `ZimmRecentlyViewedRail`,
5	 * `ProductScroller`, or nothing at all. `ZimmRecentlyViewedRail`, `ProductScroller`,
6	 * `useRecentlyViewedHistory`, `useRecentlyViewedProductFetch`, and `selectRecentlyViewedCard` are
7	 * all mocked at the smallest surface — their own internals already have their own coverage
8	 * elsewhere (`zimmRecentlyViewedRail/index.test.tsx`, `useRecentlyViewedHistory.test.ts`,
9	 * `recentlyViewedProductFetch.test.ts`, `recentlyViewedCard.test.ts`; base `ProductScroller` is
10	 * untouched vendor code).
11	 *
12	 * **Revised 2026-09-08, build plan §2 "Interim data source"** — the Recently-Viewed branch no
13	 * longer reads `recommendations.recs` (Einstein's own response) at all; it reads
14	 * `recentlyViewedIds` off `useRecentlyViewedHistory` and real product data off
15	 * `useRecentlyViewedProductFetch` instead. Mocks and fixtures below were rewritten to match:
16	 * `useRecentlyViewedGate` is gone, and the Recently-Viewed-branch tests build their product
17	 * fixtures with a real `id` field (`ShopperProductsTypes.Product`'s own shape) instead of the old
18	 * Einstein-merged `productId`. The "any other recommender" test is otherwise unaffected — it still
19	 * feeds `ProductScroller` from a real Einstein-shaped `recommendations` object, since only the
20	 * Recently-Viewed branch's data source changed.
21	 */
